                'content' => "A careful harvest can be ruined by careless handling in an afternoon, and the grower who manages the post-harvest keeps the grade the field earned, while the grower who does not sells the field's care at the price of the store's neglect. The chain has four links: harvest, collection, sorting, and storage, and the chain is only as strong as the link that was rushed.\n\nHarvest at the right maturity for the market: green for the fresh market, mature for copra and oil, and never too early or too late for the grade the buyer pays for, because the nut harvested at the wrong maturity sells at the wrong price however well it is handled after. Harvest with a pole or by hand, lower the bunch rather than dropping it, and never throw a nut to the ground, because the nut that falls far is the nut that cracks and spoils, and the cracked nut is the loss that no handling can recover.\n\nCollect quickly and cool. Move the harvest from the field to the collection point within hours, not days, and keep it out of the sun on the way, because wet, hot nuts in a sack are nuts already on the way to mold. The load should be dry, shaded, and moving, and the farmer who builds the collection routine into the harvest day is the farmer whose nuts arrive at the store still good, while the farmer who leaves the harvest in the field overnight is the farmer who sells mold for oil.\n\nSort at the collection point: separate the sound from the damaged, the large from the small, and the fresh from the old. Grading at the farm gate is what turns a mixed harvest into a saleable grade, and the buyer who sees a graded lot pays the grade price rather than the guess price, which is the difference between a profit and a compromise. The sort that takes an hour at the gate saves the whole lot from the buyer's discount.\n\nFinally, store clean and dry: off the ground, away from rain, and away from chemicals and fuel that taint the nut. The nut stored well keeps its oil and its value, and the grower who handles the harvest with care from pole to store is the grower whose grade survives the journey to the buyer, and the grade that survives the journey is the grade that earns the return buyer next season.",
